      "side": 1,
      "message": "This device has ~30 registers covering ~48 bytes of address space, and the read and write functions are starting to get pretty tedious. I would suggest storing the register values as just an array of bytes that you index by the register offset and just taking that offset directly in the read and write functions.\n\nYou can still check for specific register offsets to add specific handling for particular registers.",
      "revId": "ae0ee78260c79f5d1c538fbd39b864dd79e3e679",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
